## The open top edge — the span rule and the fork rule (26.09, LND2 + LND3)

LND2 (report `Trials/Runs/tree-open-top-edge-report.md`, uncommitted): the span marks slide to
the limb's own open top edge — `PlantTree.BestLandingSpanPoint` walks outward from the mid
(t 0.5 -> 0.95 in 0.05 steps) and takes the first point whose claw band reads `LandingSkyMinM`
0.12 of open air; a limb with no open point keeps the most open point found. The read: a
mark's seat plane is the top face of the piece it presses on (`OwnWoodFaceY`), the window is
read at the bird's own three claw columns (`LandingSkyBand` 0.03) via `LandingSkyAt`, and a
mark's sky is the smallest of the three. Six of the nine spans read 0.12 (slots 7/9/11/12/13/14);
the read rides in the run rows (`landingSkyOpenCount` / `landingSkyBestM` / `landingSkyBestSlot`)
and `<label>_sky.csv` / `_wood.csv`.

LND3 (report `Trials/Runs/tree-fork-rule-report.md`, uncommitted): THE FORK RULE —
`PlantTree.BestLandingForkPoint` (:13327) walks INWARD from the parent's tip (t 1.00 -> 0.55 in
the same 0.05 steps) and takes the first open point; a parent with no open point keeps the tip
(a fork is not traded for a merely less closed point). The walk runs on a DYNAMIC parent only
(`PlantTree.cs:13028`): the static folded trunk's order-1 forks stay on its tip and dedupe with
the trunk-top mark — none on the trunk's body. MEASURED price: the fork's own crotch cannot be
opened (a child or a neighbour closes the band at 0.0077-0.0177 above the seat plane at the six
tips — the fork's dose and its closed window are ONE fact, the crotch's rise); five of the six
parents offer no open point at all; the one move is slot 5 (fork, Wood_2_9) to t 0.80 —
(+0.3628675, -0.1055751), sky 0.12/0.12/0.12, `landingSkyOpenCount` 6 -> 7, `landingSkyBestSlot`
7 -> 5. The control rows are byte-identical (0 moved, `_joints.csv` md5 identical); the loaded
mark (0.5 kg) bends 7.97 mm, peak 21.59 mm, rebound 0.52 mm; the probe 16/16 triggers, 0 solid
contacts. The LEAF DOOR is a crown-recipe question, not a ring one: the leaf plates sit on the
twigs' distal halves (clusters at along 0.42-0.88), the same region every open top edge needs,
and five of the six open span marks stay leaf-refused by the bird's own gate.

